    "height": 221,
    "help": {
      "default": "A breakpoint envelope, drawn rather than dialled.\n\nDrag a point to move it; it stays between its neighbours, because\nthe horizontal axis is time. Hold alt (option) and click in the plot\nto add a point there. Hold ctrl (control or command) and click a\npoint to remove it, or right click it. Two points is the minimum.\n\nStraight joins the points with lines. Smooth draws a curve through\nevery point. Bezier is the same curve with a handle pair hung on\nevery point: drag a handle to pull the curve as it leaves or arrives,\nand the opposite handle follows so the line stays smooth through the\npoint. Ctrl click a handle to put it back to automatic. The points\nare the same in every mode, so switching modes never moves one.\n\nLength is the time for the whole envelope. The vertical lines are one\nsecond apart, and the yellow line is the playhead while it runs.\n\nPoints is how many are live. Raising it splits the longest stretch of\nthe curve; lowering it removes the point that bends the line least,\nnever an end.\n\nTrigger CV starts it on a rising edge. The CV output is the envelope\nitself; the Output is the Input scaled by it, so the device can be\nused either as a control source or inline on a signal. The last\nvalue is held to the end rather than dropping to zero.",
      "key": "plugin.33.panel.help"
    },
    "poll": [
      "PLAYHEAD"
    ],
